␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ommand-line arguments
; ============================================================================
; MAC (macro assembler) port of MCPDONE.C, feature for feature:
;
;   printf("MCP-TOOL-COMPLETED");
;   for (i = 1; i < argc; i++)
;       printf(" %s", argv[i]);
;   printf("\n");
;
; The CP/M CCP places the command tail at 0080H: a length byte followed by
; the raw characters typed after the program name (already upper-cased). We
; reproduce the C argv behaviour by walking that tail, collapsing runs of
; spaces, and emitting exactly one leading space before each argument token.
;
; This version uses Digital Research MAC macros for the BDOS calls. Build it
; with the macro assembler rather than ASM:
;
;   mac mcpdone        ->  MCPDONE.HEX (plus .PRN/.SYM)
;   load mcpdone       ->  MCPDONE.COM
;
; MAC constraints: symbols unique in first 6 chars; ports in decimal.
; ============================================================================

BDOS    EQU     5               ; CP/M BDOS entry point
FPRCHR  EQU     2               ; BDOS func 2: console output (char in E)
FPRSTR  EQU     9               ; BDOS func 9: print '$'-terminated string
TAILLN  EQU     0080H           ; command tail length byte
TAILCH  EQU     0081H           ; first character of the command tail
SPACE   EQU     ' '

; -- macro: invoke a BDOS function -----------------------------------------
DOS     MACRO   FUNC
        MVI     C,FUNC
        CALL    BDOS
        ENDM

; -- macro: print a '$'-terminated string at label STR ---------------------
PRINT   MACRO   STR
        LXI     D,STR
        DOS     FPRSTR
        ENDM

; -- macro: print the character in E (preserves HL and BC) -----------------
EMITCH  MACRO
        PUSH    H
        PUSH    B
        DOS     FPRCHR
        POP     B
        POP     H
        ENDM

        ORG     0100H           ; CP/M trans; ============================================================================
; FT - File Transfer "Get" client for the Altair 8800 (8080 macro assembler)
; ============================================================================
; MAC (Digital Research macro assembler) port of FT.C, feature for feature:
;
;   ft                     -> print help/usage banner
;   ft -g <filename>       -> download <filename> from the Remote FT Server
;   ft <anything else>     -> "Invalid arguments" message
;
; The download path is the original path sent to the server (e.g.
; SUBDIR/FOO.C); the file is saved locally under its basename (FOO.C). The
; transfer uses host I/O ports 21 (command/status) and 22 (data), exactly as
; the C version:
;
;   OUT 21,1   start a filename transfer (SETFN)
;   OUT 22,c   send each filename character, then OUT 22,0 (NUL terminator)
;   IN  21     poll status: 0=IDLE 1=DATA 2=EOF 3=BUSY 255=ERR
;   OUT 21,3   request the next data chunk (GETCH)
;   IN  22     read the chunk length byte (0 means 256), then that many bytes
;   OUT 21,4   close the transfer (CLOSE)
;
; Received bytes are written to a freshly created CP/M file via the BDOS
; sequential-write calls. fopen write mode is reproduced as delete-then-make.
; Two transfer modes, selected on the command line:
;   -g  <file>  text mode: incoming CR is stripped and LF is expanded to
;               CR LF, so the saved file always has canonical CP/M line
;               endings (works for LF-only and CRLF sources alike); a single
;               ^Z end-of-text marker is written and the final record is
;               NUL-padded. This is what SUBMIT/MAC/CC expect.
;   -gb <file>  binary mode: bytes are written verbatim with no ^Z; the final
;               partial record is padded with NUL (00H).
;
; One intentional deviation from FT.C: the byte counter is a 32-bit value
; here rather than the C version's 16-bit int, so the "Done (<n> bytes)"
; total does not wrap at 65536 for files larger than 64K.
;
; Buil~Ј Ёn}Ј!␀␀(#|µ(Ёnю&␀#лi`~Ј(	Ёn€&␀#Ёu€Ёn}Ј!␀␀(#&␀#ЁuьЁtэЁnю&␀Ё^ьЁVэ&␀ЁuьЁtэЁuю√сЁn€&␀ЁщЁб…ЁеЁ!␀␀Ё9!щ€9щ!]␀ЁuюЁt€~Ј(ЁnюЁf€~ю  !␀√э	!␀␀ЁuэЁNюЁF€Ё~эю“ъ	i`лo&␀~ю?(;i`лЁnэ&␀n&␀ЁuыЁtьЁnэлЁnЁfn&␀}жo≈ўЁnыЁfьўеў—ЅЈнR(!␀␀Ёnэ&␀#ЁuыЁtьЁuэ√Щ	!␀ЁщЁб…ЁеЁ!␀␀Ё9!з€9щЁ6н␀Ё6о␀Ё6с␀!␀ЁuлЁtмЁuпЁtр!␀␀ЁuтЁNЁFЁ~тю03o&␀еЁебу€—еo&␀#лi`n&␀}жoе—бsЁnт&␀#ЁuйЁtкЁuт√6
